==============================================================================
5. AC-006 / BL-003: listGuardedFiles' observable behaviour is byte-identical
==============================================================================

The weak version of this claim is "listGuardedFiles(...) deepEquals
listGuardedFilesWithDiagnostics(...).files", which after the change is true by
construction (the wrapper returns that very array) and therefore proves
nothing about PRESERVATION. The strong version -- comparing the post-change
function against the PRE-change function -- was measured instead.

Method: a harness (session scratchpad, not committed) imports the compiled
`listGuardedFiles` and runs it over a fixed battery of 25 fixture cases,
emitting a stable JSON document recording, per case, the raw return value, the
sorted return value, the length, and whether the call threw. It was run TWICE
against identical fixtures: once at the pristine 9091f96b tree BEFORE the new
test file existed and BEFORE any src/ edit, and once after the implementation
landed.

The 25 cases:
  * 6 real-repository directories the 3 call sites actually scan
    (docs/review-tickets, docs/workflow-improvements, reports/quality-gate,
    reports/impl-review, reports/retrospective, reports/task-review).
    `specs` and `reports/implementation` are deliberately EXCLUDED because
    this task itself writes files under both, so their listing legitimately
    changes between the two runs; excluding them is disclosed here rather than
    quietly omitted.
  * the exact synthetic fixtures quality-report.test.ts, review-ticket.test.ts
    and report-lookup.ts's scan shape build (cases B, B2 trailing-slash,
    B3 parent-directory, C, D)
  * nested-walk cases (E, E2)
  * every guard-failure class: not-found, outside-allowlist, denylisted
    basename, parent traversal, absolute path, empty path, backslash path,
    file-not-a-directory, symlink escaping the allowlist (F, G, H, I1-I4, J, N)
  * both mid-walk failure shapes: dangling symlink (statSync) and a mode-0o000
    subdirectory (readdirSync) -- cases L and M

